ety outcome or admitted Core/MIR. Missing review can reject, and audit-only records without an approval gate. Imported certificate/unsafe summaries refer to already-built dependency packages Q; current package P emits its own local safety products before its later packaging. P's own published certificate is never its classification input. Additional SAFE2-SAFE5 classification consumes complete specialized access/initialization/alias/lifetime/region/generation/linear/transfer facts and obligations, exact current profile/provider availability and existing subject-bound proof/audit decisions. Bind each permitted dynamic check to the operation, attached state, emitted identity/location, declared failure and introduced effects before violation; actual check/failure execution remains later evidence. Missing dynamic machinery requires the specific source rule's proof or refusal, with an explicit audited unsafe alternative only where that rule and profile/mode policy permit it. SAFE3 normal-borrow and SAFE4 safe arena-use refusals survive. Unsafe candidates and supplied verdicts confer neither a fifth outcome nor accepted MIR; existing required specialist review remains separate from audit-only records. Additional L10/L18 disposition covers the exact source/provider replacement, raw/MMIO/foreign wrapper and privileged-forget obligations. Preserve the actual type/ownership/effect/grant, map/width/volatile/order/lifetime, failure/cleanup and source-bound proof/audit inputs; provider trust, a wrapper label or another subject's certificate cannot admit the operation. Candidate, policy-required specialist and final four-outcome stages remain distinct; audit-only gains no approval gate. Additional SAFE8 classification combines actual race/capture/share/guard/message facts with checked effects, provider contracts, typed schemas and profile/grant premises. Choose only proven-safe, valid preventive runtime synchronization, rejected or explicit audited unsafe-island; a debug detector