orbidden labels, handler forms and modes before combined handler legality. Runtime execution, final Effects5 conformance and conditional new stable adoption are not prerequisites for checking existing source/profile contracts. A fixture interpreter never supplies an ambient permissive profile. Additional L11/SAFE8 profile compatibility consumes early actual hardware-clocked or GPU kernel/host-boundary definitions when those profiles are selected, alongside real provider/runtime support. Distinguish all thirteen source families and nine explicit L11 profile cases, refusing unsupported scheduling, blocking, shared mutation or target primitives. Source definitions precede their later emitted/device/simulation outcomes; final domain/backend conformance is no profile-check start gate. Physical executor/target limits survive project-accounting removal without input/work quotas or hidden host threads. Additional provider compatibility checks complete declared contracts/effects/targets/trust/isolation and revocation or permitted static-lifetime substitutes against the actual profile before final selection. Early declaration/support products precede this verdict; runtime initialization and owner conformance follow it. Ambient permission is explicit, untrusted isolation must actually exist, and no trusted signature or runtime fallback repairs compiler illegality. Additional L12 profile checker consumes early P requests and actual Q source declarations with fixed target/provider/isolation contracts, then supplies the actual profile verdict before affected evaluation or generated admission. Preserve all nine explicit cases: pure portable core, auditable granted hosted services, declared native targets, mandatory hermetic kernel/firmware/hardware with unmodeled-facility refusal, distributed workflow records, AI identity/retention/review and checked meta IR. Early definitions precede their own later conformance; no host fallback repairs a rejected profile. Additional joint macro 