 analysis. Derive initialization, owner/borrow/region/allocator/range/sharing and linear/privileged-forget obligations from those typed/source/provider/grant facts, preserving safe/unsafe alternatives and source-specific static refusals. These facts precede verified MIR and later actual provider/API execution. Additional L6 capture analysis consumes actual verified Core structure and early inferred direct/latent actions. Derive the selected resource/type/lifetime/transfer/cloning premises independently for Effects3 before its combined handler decision; existing later memory-policy analysis still consumes checked Effects3. Captured linear resources, borrows, raw pointers, interrupt state, locks and FFI frames need actual profile-valid transfer or refusal, not a candidate flag treated as proof. No final handler interpretation, whole Effects5 acceptance or later target layout is required before producing these source-bound facts. Additional SAFE8 fact analysis consumes actual typed ownership/alias/control, early direct/latent effects, message and selected hardware/GPU source definitions plus declared synchronization contracts. Derive conflicts, moves, scoped borrow expiry, immutable representation/hidden cache mutation and GPU barrier/address-space facts before combined safety and handler admission; a selected Runtime transfer primitive can later witness execution, not supply an asserted race-free premise. Detached tasks still cannot capture non-static borrows, even with an owner. Message schema definitions are available before delivery and do not require later actor execution or whole Schema migration. Additional joint macro memory/ownership analysis consumes actual generated operations, captures, lifetimes and caller-profile facts with complete origins. Compiler-generated code undergoes the same ordinary analysis as handwritten code, including facet/schema/FFI/workflow/hardware/compiler output where claimed. No early typed result, declaration or assigned safe flag replaces actual owner decisions; preserve actual held native/provider boundaries. Additional complete C3 ownership boundary uses actual source/generated identities and current fact conditions for syntax-derived captures and memory operations. The analysis owner computes ownership/lifetime/initialization facts and regeneration; Syntax transports and invalidates them when an affecting transformation occurs. Verified carrier shape or assigned ownership metadata is not the analysis result.",
