ncy semantic-change criterion only: where an actual stable concurrency contract changes, consume the affected compiler/safety/provider/runtime/library/hardware/GPU/workflow/AI results and required compatibility/performance evidence before that adoption. Early candidate definitions may be analyzed only in an actually permitted context; this adds no experiment permission or ordinary unchanged-contract development gate. Keep existing independent safety-review, effect registration and all exact review subjects distinct; no sealed review is consumed again. Additional conditional macro-semantics adoption consumes actual affected syntax schema, public definition/version, macro safety/diagnostic/formatter/LSP/inspector and bootstrap-equivalence results before a stable language-change decision. Preserve the exact existing Evolution predicate and compatibility/edition scope. This is conditional adoption of changed semantics; compatible implementation replacement and ordinary unchanged-contract development do not require a new adoption, experiment or routine review ticket. Construction of candidate evidence does not wait for its own later adoption. Additional complete C3 conditional compatibility review consumes actual affected syntax identity/schema, fact/metadata/origin, serialization, formatter/LSP/diagnostic and claimed-stage comparisons when public semantics change. Preserve existing tracked-change/review/adoption rules and raw-candidate versus stable-support admission boundaries. Ordinary unchanged-contract implementation acquires no generic new review ceremony or future release prerequisite. Additional complete L3/C5 conditional compatibility review consumes actual affected binding/module/public API/profile/diagnostic, package/cache, macro/type/effect, documentation/LSP and bootstrap-order results when namespace/module semantics change. Preserve the existing package compatibility review and conformance updates, versioned tracked change and stable adoption boundary. Ordinary unchanged-contract implementation and restoring existing criteria add no generic review ceremony or final-release prerequisite. Complete L2/C6 compatibility consumption applies only to the existing conditional semantic-change/adoption subject. Consume actual affected syntax/type/effect/safety/compiler/backend/runtime/test/documentation products and current lowering-rule/diagnostic/invalidation evidence before that adoption claim. Restoring unchanged declared requirements and ordinary fixture development do not create a new approval ceremony. Frozen C6/profile74 receipts retain exact scope; current source, implementation, independent acceptance and integration remain separate. Complete L5/C7 type-form adoption uses the unchanged conditional Evolution producer: actual artifact-schema updates, fixtures and affected effect/memory/profile/MIR/backend/schema/AI/library/documentation consumers precede stable use of a changed type form. Ordinary development against unchanged contracts adds no approval ceremony. Earlier finite receipts stay frozen; source restoration and current staged interfaces confer no implementation, publication, independent acceptance or integration credit.",
