     "C9-selected actual ownership obligations, profile/provider check availability and explicit unsupported cases, grants, subject-bound checked proof/audit evidence and declared dynamic-check metadata/failure contract. Classify each operation before affected MIR; authority, ownership validity and safety proof stay distinct. This task decides legal check/proof/rejection/unsafe conditions; actual provider check/failure execution is separate evidence consumed by final boundary/conformance results. Additional C10-selected inputs are the real Core operation/control-flow and generated-origin/unsafe/taint products, actual type/effect solutions, exact artifact/trust decisions, package digest/schema/compiler/profile/target/certificate validation and build-effect/import provenance, numeric/EFIR/mode contracts and independently checked applicable math claims, plus admitted model/tool/schema/taint/review and workflow replay/idempotency policy products. Numeric proof checking applies when such a proof is claimed; the operation can instead retain a legal check or reject. Domain policy contracts are available before actual model/tool/workflow execution; a producer's whole result or final publication is not a classification prerequisite. Specialized SAFE analyzers remain with their existing owners; grants, verified imported evidence and safe-wrapper audit approval remain distinct from supplied labels. Additional SAFE1/SAFE6-selected inputs include the distinct actual GOV9 specialist unsafe-audit decision for a policy-required reviewed island, with source/island/wrapper/profile/target, reviewer/evidence/expiry and stale/revalidation identity. The Evolution owner retains this decision separately from generic GOV4 security review, with conditional GOV3/STD20 evidence for standard-library islands. Candidate unsafe inventory/audit and wrapper proof/check products are produced first; final reviewed-unsafe eligibility consumes the actual required decision. A candidate is not a fifth safety outcome or admitted Core/MIR. Missing review can reject, and audit-only records without an approval gate. Imported certificate/unsafe summaries refer to already-built dependency packages Q; current package P emits its own local safety products before its later packaging. P's own published certificate is never its classification input. Additional SAFE2-SAFE5 classification consumes complete specialized access/initialization/alias/lifetime/region/generation/linear/transfer facts and obligations, exact current profile/provider availability and existing subject-bound proof/audit decisions. Bind each permitted dynamic check to the operation, attached state, emitted identity/location, declared failure and introduced effects before violation; actual check/failure execution remains later evidence. Missing dynamic machinery requires the specific source rule's proof or refusal, with an explicit audited unsafe alternative only where that rule and profile/mode policy permit it. SAFE3 normal-borrow and SAFE4 safe arena-use refusals survive. Unsafe candidates and supplied verdicts confer neither a fifth outcome nor accepted MIR; existing required specialist review remains separate from audit-only records. Additional L10/L18 disposition covers the exact source/provider replacement, raw/MMIO/foreign wrapper and privileged-forget obligations. Preserve the actual type/ownership/effect/grant, map/width/volatile/order/lifetime, failure/cleanup and source-bound proof/audit inputs; provider trust, a wrapper label or another subject's certificate cannot admit the operation. Candidate, policy-required specialist and final four-outcome stages remain distinct; audit-only gains no approval gate. Additional SAFE8 classification combines actual race/capture/share/guard/message facts with checked effects, provider contracts, typed schemas and profile/grant premises. Choose only proven-safe, valid preventive runtime synchronization, rejected or explicit audited unsafe-island; a debug detector