g checks where preservation fails. C3 verification and metadata cannot replace later MIR/runtime semantic enforcement or establish seed retirement. Complete L5/C7 safety handoff preserves actual current resource/layout/schema/dynamic/conversion facts, their proof/check/reject/unsafe verdicts and complete invalidation into MIR and selected runtime metadata. Every consuming stage reconstructs required private-entry/key-domain/loop premises rather than trusting an earlier solved flag. Required checks and failure semantics survive actual later lowering/execution; their declared records are not execution evidence.",
