     "Selected L6 resumable-error execution consumes actual typed handler/request/response/result/resume facts, combined handler legality, exact grants, valid capture/transfer facts, early replay obligations and selected service support. Runtime3 supplies the actual selected continuation/resource primitive result, not completed acceptance of every async/generator/memory case. Runtime2's early panic/failure/cleanup contract is available before Runtime3 service use; later real resume/abort/finalization/cleanup traces follow execution. Reject invalid payload/results, unsafe or repeated affine resume and finalized/cancelled/closed reuse. A generic error record or completed flag is not execution, and final teardown or final compiler release is not an ordinary start gate. Additional R6 cancellation/failure cleanup consumes actual selected task/resource transitions and the early cleanup/observability contract, then produces actual exact linear release, handler completion and preserved failure/diagnostic records. Runtime5's early event/redaction sink interface precedes those records; its later integrated enforcement trace consumes them. Cleanup cannot be replaced by GC/process exit, a cancellation flag or a promised handler, nor made to wait for its own later whole-program teardown result. Additional L15 startup checks real required provider presence, selected versions, scopes against actual grants, contract agreement, profile/target compatibility and enabled safety/audit requirements before user code. Consume selected linked/loaded implementations and installed gates; an early initialization contract may precede later per-program startup evidence. Missing providers fail before user execution unless a declared compatible fallback passes the same checks. A manifest or assigned initialized flag cannot prove startup, and no hidden fallback or physical execution authority is introduced. Additional L12 explicit runtime-fallback boundary consumes only an actually source-permitted fallback Q with ordinary checked effects/grants/profile/target and selected implemented services before execution. Early failure/cleanup/service contracts precede compile-time checking; actual Q startup/execution/cleanup follows it where the source case claims behavior. No silent fallback from fuel, failed proof, invalid constant, phase or profile illegality is introduced, and no whole Runtime completion or held native/provider action gates unrelated pure evaluation. Complete L2/C6 execution consumes actual admitted Core or emitted program for the selected execution path, preserving truthiness, one-branch choice, ordered arguments/initializers/body, lexical/capture/recur/def/var/mutation and typed error/panic/cleanup semantics. Early panic/error/service primitives can be implemented before compiling their consumers; interpreter execution needs no fictitious native artifact, while compiled execution requires its real emitted input. Normalize host nulls/exceptions and retain actual source/generated failure traces. No new Core interpreter is assigned and no held execution is authorized. Complete L7 selected execution uses actual admitted Core or emitted program for its chosen interpreter/compiled path. Evaluate the scrutinee once, skip guard/body on structural failure, run each reached guard once after binding, continue on false and preserve non-returning transfer and resource cleanup. Early execution/error contracts precede caller compilation; actual traces follow. An interpreter needs no fictitious native artifact and this adds no second evaluator or held execution permission.",
