 for the service that they call. Additional complete concurrency handoff has early and later products. Export actual checked source-derived task/scope/capture/move/sync/atomic/schema/replay/check/unsafe obligations before MIR and target consumers. Later consume actual verified MIR, affected Opt/Lower preservation, selected GPU/HDL artifacts, Runtime/library execution and enforcement traces for the claimed end-to-end result; these later results cannot be prerequisites for their own input facts. Preserve source sequential-consistency defaults unless an explicit governing profile/library permits weaker order, target scope/fence/alignment support and affected invalidation. Record copying or a supplied safe flag is not preservation evidence. Additional provider preservation exports actual checked effect/capability/provider/grant/phase/scope/lifetime/trust/isolation obligations before MIR and target use, then consumes exact installed-gate, startup, build/runtime and invalidation results for the claimed end-to-end case. Bind actual artifacts to source/compiler/profile/target/policy identities, invalidate changed assumptions, and preserve redacted diagnostics and audit records. Later execution and cache reuse cannot supply earlier legality or authority; imported Q inputs remain distinct from P's later output evidence. Additional joint macro downstream preservation consumes actual ordinary Q decisions and syntax-origin/safety/taint/unsafe/authority products, then retains them into MIR, selected lowering and runtime artifacts. Reject lost capture/SAFE6/sink/profile obligations or forged generated-safe labels. This is actual preservation/composition, not reimplementation of macro execution or a new full-runtime construction gate. Additional complete C3 checked handoff retains actual source/generated maps, hygiene, producer/version/invalidation and ordinary profile/safety facts through syntax-derived Core/MIR interfaces. Require actual owner replacement/regeneration or surviving checks where preservation fails. C3 verification and metadata cannot replace later MIR/runtime semantic enforcement or establish seed retirement. Complete L5/C7 safety handoff preserves actual current resource/layout/schema/dynamic/conversion facts, their proof/check/reject/unsafe verdicts and complete invalidation into MIR and selected runtime metadata. Every consuming stage reconstructs required private-entry/key-domain/loop premises rather than trusting an earlier solved flag. Required checks and failure semantics survive actual later lowering/execution; their declared records are not execution evidence. Complete L7 handoff preserves real checked pattern control, validation/check obligations, move/borrow/linear and effect/order/replay facts into current MIR and selected runtime products. Bind every table and source/generated origin to the same subject, invalidate changed premises and reject lost obligations. A decision skeleton or evaluation label is not actual analysis or installed enforcement.",
