     "Additional provider type boundary supplies actual capability id, provider contract, scope, phase, lifetime, thread-safety and revocation facts from source/declarations before combined legality. Passing/storing a capability as data need not perform its eventual effect. Type correctness never proves grant issuance, allowed scope use, successful provider startup or full C7 acceptance; selected schema shapes precede actual codecs where serialization is used. Additional L12 type handoff supplies real early solved P expression/callable/capability/allocation/capture and fixed target-query facts before evaluation. Later consume actual constants/generated Q and owner solutions for Q's ordinary type/representability and invalidation result. Type-level evaluation and generated protocol/schema cases cannot require Q's own final type/layout result as their earlier input. Keep target ABI rules distinct from derived Q layout, and current C7 publication/whole-source acceptance unaltered; supplied type names or passed flags do not prove values or grants. Additional joint macro type handoff exposes real available P/expected-type facts where an engine uses them, then checks actual Q with ordinary solutions and representability/invalidation. Earlier typed-engine rejection must match or improve a later required diagnostic, while effect/authority/memory/profile/safety checks remain. A type-shaped syntax record is not a solved fact or full C7 acceptance; preserve current C7 restrictions. Additional complete C3 type-fact handoff consumes actual serialized solutions/layout requirements and owner invalidation conditions from Types4, valid syntax-derived references and real Syntax lifecycle decisions. Types retains solving, semantic freshness and regeneration; Syntax retains carrier/transform invalidation. Preserve source/profile/ownership/effect references and reject stale facts before downstream use. Early source syntax verification does not depend on its later typed result. Additional complete L3/C5 type handoff uses actual resolved/verified bindings, selected legal imports/graph and current namespace definition/type records. Retain real solved type/protocol/call identities and separate inferred versus declared facts before Effects/Legality/MIR. Reject stale exports, substituted bindings and inconsistent module/checker facts; an early namespace map is not final type or authority acceptance.",
