  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-profile-compliance-fixtures` Execute profile compliance fixtures\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST4](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/193-test4-profile-compliance-test-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute profile compliance fixtures runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source testing/test4/allocation-runtime: Test profile allocation, memory, dynamic eval, reflection, GC, runtime and host-service assumptions wherever profile rules mention them. Concrete acceptance: In each applicable profile exercise allowed and forbidden allocation/memory/eval/reflection/GC/runtime/host-service cases; fail any undocumented hosted assumption or missing runtime-legality result. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test4/capability-legality: Test capability legality separately per profile. Concrete acceptance: For each declared profile execute granted and missing/forbidden-grant cases; fail a profile result that inherits a different profile's authority. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test4/compatibility: Detect and reject unresolved compatibility conflicts in multi-profile project/package fixtures. Concrete acceptance: Compose multi-profile packages with a deliberate incompatible boundary; require a compatibility diagnostic and no falsely passing combined package. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test4/delegation: Record target-specific delegation only where permitted by the profile, with profile legality results in artifacts. Concrete acceptance: Remove a delegation artifact or choose a target service outside the profile's permitted delegation; reject and identify the violated rule. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test4/profile-legality: Exercise each named profile with allowed/checked/delegated/rejected categories, accepting allowed behavior, rejecting forbidden services at compile time where possible and honoring required diagnostic severity; no default hosted assumptions in stricter profiles. Concrete acceptance: Exercise allowed/checked/delegated/rejected categories for every named profile; fail rejected allowed behavior, accepted forbidden services, wrong diagnostic severity or missing compile-time rejection where possible. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test4/report: Emit profile compliance, profile/target matrix, positive/negative results, capability/runtime legality and artifact delegation reports. Concrete acceptance: Remove profile/target matrix cells, negative results, capability/runtime legality or delegation records; fail missing claimed coverage rather than counting unspecified cells as success. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. This producer sup