  "- [ ] `build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-dependency-aware-caching-and-invalidation` Implement dependency-aware caching and invalidation\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Pass cache](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/pass_cache.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Reuse on equal inputs; rebuild on source, compiler, grant, policy or target changes\n\n\n<!-- build-canonical-cache-conditions:start -->\nApply the [complete incremental-compilation source criteria](plan.md#complete-incremental-compilation-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; current independent review and implementation acceptance are pending. Existing criterion fragments remain in place.\n\nSource compiler/c16/cache-revalidation: Reuse stage-specific entries only after producing-pass/schema/version/facts/policy/dependency/diagnostic validation, retaining provenance and invalidation records. Concrete acceptance: Change producer pass version, schema, preserved facts, profile/target, policy, dependency or diagnostic schema separately; reject stale reuse and record the actual affected revalidation/recomputation, keeping prior provenance. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source compiler/c16/proof-reuse: Reuse proofs/certificates only when complete claim/input/assumption/context/invalidation conditions match; require a mapping when node identity changes but semantics survive. Concrete acceptance: Change each claim/input/assumption/profile/target/compiler/provider/package/invalidation premise, and change a node ID without a proof mapping; reject reuse or reprove, retaining residual checks until evidence is valid. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source compiler/c16/r