oducts and invalidation. Checked macro/extension program P and early candidate/type/layout facts must be available before the relevant execution, while generated caller Q is checked afterward. Later phases inspect immutable earlier artifacts; normalization/memoization retains original spans and generated-origin chains and produces new identities rather than mutating prior ones. Preserve the existing D1/C1/C5/C6 ordering decision as unresolved under its current architecture owner instead of inventing a new pipeline. Build owns graph scheduling and immutable products, the compiler API owns pass semantics/observable boundaries, and semantic owners supply actual decisions. Reject illegal order, missing facts, unauthorized target/extension work and lost or mutated provenance with real before/after artifacts.\n<!-- compile-time-source-phases:end -->",
