  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-library-conformance-fixtures` Execute library conformance fixtures\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST7](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/196-test7-standard-library-test-strategy.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute library conformance fixtures runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source testing/test7/availability: Validate per-API/module profile and target availability without importing hosted assumptions into stricter profiles. Concrete acceptance: Run API/module fixtures across declared profile/target availability; reject unsupported availability claims and hosted-only dependencies in stricter profiles. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test7/capability-denial: Test effectful API required effects and missing-capability failures; IO/network/database/platform APIs require mock and capability-denial fixtures. Concrete acceptance: For effectful IO/network/database/platform APIs run recorded/mock success and missing-capability cases; assert denial before the operation and fail ambient grants. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test7/properties: Property-test collection, string, numeric and schema APIs. Concrete acceptance: Execute declared collection/string/numeric/schema invariants and known counterexamples through real APIs; fail an absent oracle, un