  "- [ ] `mir/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/mir5-gate-downstream-consumption` mir/5: Gate downstream consumption\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Run actual verifier on constructed and mutated MIR; retain positive and negative artifacts for malformed flow, missing facts, target leaks and invalid origins before Opt/Lower consumption.\n\n\n<!-- mir-canonical-consumption:start -->\nApply the [complete MIR source criteria](plan.md#complete-mir-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; current independent review and implementation acceptance are pending.\n\nC11 consumption criterion gravity/mir-verification-after-transform (Open): Run the actual MIR verifier after construction and after each transformation that may invalidate invariants. Bind each result to the exact current module, transformation and fact identities; reject failed, missing or stale verification before public Opt/Lower consumption. Required outputs: before/after MIR, actual verifier reports, preserved/invalidated/recomputed fact records and positive/negative consumer-gate results. Runtime checks remain safety-referenced MIR operations and generic dead-code elimination cannot remove them; check elision consumes the applicable checked PERF10 evidence with subject binding and proof/guard dominance, or retains the check/rejects. Exercise invalidating transforms, malformed flow/missing types/effects/safety/origins, invalid profile facts, invalid anchors, unchecked source/core/MIR delivery and bounds-check erasure without surviving proof. Target-family consumption also uses actual declared profile/target/runtime-provider support; the backend cannot legalize rejected MIR or redefine generic op semantics. The owning optimizer/lowerer and proof checker supply their actual products; MIR gate ownership does not implement them. Ordinary source editing and negative-fixture preparation do not require release or migration 