  "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution` Connect distributed/AI replay and interactive execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Recorded nondeterminism, replay equality, no undeclared duplicated external effect, REPL grant denial. R6/R7/R8/R9: topology/provider/event-log/state/message schemas; durable idempotency, timeout/retry/cancellation/failure/compensation records; migration or rejection of replay-incompatible code/topology/schema changes; model/provider/prompt provenance, output and sink validation, policy-recorded provider substitution, typed tool contracts with caller/callee grants and policy-required human review, memory/retrieval privacy/retention/deletion/taint controls and secret redaction; R7/R8 replay-required segments return recorded model/tool/retrieval/memory/review decisions or reject a missing record. R6 concurrency fixtures accept an authorized graph-declared replay-safe repetition where no R7/R8 recorded-output obligation applies; the declaration never grants authority or overrides those recorded-output obligations. Interactive forms and generated code pass the ordinary compiler checks before execution; session manifests, transcripts, evaluated forms, syntax/core/MIR/source snapshots capture build-affecting state or mark nonhermeticity, and hot reload invalidates stale analysis/backend/runtime/package outputs. Reject undeclared repeated external calls, live nondeterministic calls in R7/R8 recorded-output segments even with a replay-safe graph declaration, repetitions without required authority, unvalidated trusted sinks, forbidden-profile eval, hidden interactive IO and stale reload artifacts. Dependencies: Domains supplies agent/workflow contracts, Schema supplies validators/migrations, Build consumes session inputs and invalidation, Auth supplies grants and review policy. Project work