on or refusal under existing C10/SAFE15/PERF10 criteria. Keep stable machine-readable unsafe/review/wrapper/dependency records visible even when permitted, including in release/package policy, conformance, audit/documentation and language-server safety views. Supply all required safety classifications, check records, audits, proof references, diagnostics, profile-safety capability reports, generated provenance, check-erasure justifications and certificate inputs to their existing consumers. Reject lost metadata or hidden dependency unsafe behavior and revoked/wrong-source/expired evidence; this handoff owns composition, not a second analyzer, package publisher, unsafe reviewer or proof checker.\n<!-- legality-canonical-safety-root-preservation:end -->\n\n\n<!-- legality-canonical-memory-preservation:start -->\n\nApply the [complete memory-safety source criteria](plan.md#complete-memory-safety-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; finite review scope is frozen and current whole-source/composition review remains pending.\n\nSAFE2-SAFE5 memory consumer-preservation criterion (Open): Compose the existing analysis producer's actual allocation/release/range/layout/init/lifetime/borrow/region/generation/linear/transfer/cleanup/check/proof/audit/provider facts with C10, MIR, Opt, Lower/backend, Runtime and diagnostics. Actual consumers emit and execute guards, declared failure, cleanup and transfers where claimed; the original thirty producer criteria still require that evidence, not record-only substitutes. Inlining, loop changes, check elimination, escape/region inference, allocation sinking, vectorization, FFI lowering and device scheduling invalidate affected assumptions unless exact valid mappings survive; recompute/recheck or restore checks/refuse. Backends preserve actual alignment, bounds, lifetime, aliasing, volatile, atomic and allocator facts. Exact erased-check proof and residual checks follow SAFE15/PERF10, retaining source/generated and provider identities. Types/Effects/Auth/provider/profile/source/target/checker remain distinct actual inputs. This handoff owns boundary composition, never a second state analyzer, checker, backend, allocator or resource provider, and ordinary declared-interface fixtures need no whole-component or migration completion.\n<!-- legality-canonical-memory-preservation:end -->\n\n\n<!-- legality-canonical-memory-model-preservation:start -->\n\nApply the [complete source memory-model and provider criteria](plan.md#complete-source-memory-model-and-provider-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; frozen finite review does not accept the new whole-source or current composition.\n\nL10/L18 memory artifact preservation criterion (Open): Serialize actual regime/allocator/runtime/provider/version, ownership/borrow/lifetime/region/escape/init/alias/range/layout/linear/transfer/check/proof/audit and applicable device/MMIO/FFI facts into typed artifacts for their real MIR/Opt/Lower/Runtime/diagnostic consumers. Every actual transformation preserves its exact memory-safety premises or invalidates and recomputes/rechecks them, retaining a legal check or refusing unsupported use. Preserve source/generated identities, memory spaces, physical layouts/alignment, volatile/barrier/atomic order, selected allocator/releaser, safe-wrapper invariants and dependencies; target noalias/alignment/dereferenceable metadata needs current subject-bound proof. Layout/ABI/provider/backend/device-map changes cannot inherit stale proofs. Compiler and API annotations, actual linked manifests and runtime behavior must agree. Demonstrate actual accepted and refused consumer paths, proof invalidation and retained/elided checks under existing SAFE15/PERF10 obligations; this handoff neither implements the allocator nor accepts every profile/provider/backend.\n<!-- legality-canonical-memory-model-preservation:end -->\n\n\n<!-- concurrency-source-handoff:start -->\n\nApply the [complete concurrency source criteria](plan.md#complete-concurrency-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; historical finite reviews do not accept this whole-source/current implementation proposal.\n\nPreserved finite predicate conjunctions and historical source context:\n\nAllocation interface/safety/safe8/atomic-ordering (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: task/shared-location/synchronization graph and selected target/provider memory model. Required positive predicate: Require explicit supported atomic order and fences, preserving it in optimization/lowering or diagnosing unsupported targets; unchecked target-specific atomics require audit. Positive output witness: Explicit atomic order/fence/target support and preserved optimization/lowering evidence. Concrete negative case: An atomic omits memory order, requires an unsupported target fence or lowering weakens acquire/release semantics. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred.\n\nComplete concurrency preservation criterion (Open): Carry actual ownership/task/capture, synchronization graph, lock/guard, channel/actor schema, atomic operation/order/scope/alignment/target support, replay and four-outcome proof/check/unsafe facts through MIR, optimization, lowering and Runtime. Resolve source atomic order as sequentially consistent by default unless an explicit governing profile/library contract permits a weaker order; preserve relaxed, acquire, release, acquire-release and sequentially-consistent meanings, fences and target legality without importing host-language defaults. Unsupported representation is rejected or uses an explicitly allowed equivalent/audited primitive as required by its contract. Changed alias/control/lifetime/provider/target/order assumptions invalidate and recheck affected facts; metadata copying or a proof label cannot authorize check elision or weakened ordering.\n<!-- concurrency-source-handoff:end -->\n\n\n<!-- authority-source-handoff:start -->\n\nApply the [complete provider and capability source criteria](../auth-workflow/plan.md#complete-provider-and-capability-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; frozen finite reviews do not accept this whole-source/current implementation proposal.\n\nComplete authority preservation criterion (Open): Preserve actual effect/capability separation, provider selection, typed capability scope/lifetime/thread-safety/revocation, grant/policy inputs, required checks, isolation/unsafe/audit and source/generated identities through checked Core, MIR, optimization, Lower, emitted service hooks and Runtime/build consumers. Changed source/provider/version/target/profile/policy/phase/lifetime or transform assumptions invalidate affected facts and restore checks or reprove the exact obligation. Verify that denied operations cannot become permitted after transformation, deployment or older-record composition. Keep secret values out of public diagnostics/code/cache/artifact products. Actual consumer hooks and accepted/refused end-to-end products must witness preservation; copied metadata or a proof/trust/selection label is insufficient.\n<!-- authority-source-handoff:end -->\n\n\n\n<!-- legality-interop-source-handoff:start -->\n\nApply the [complete interoperability and migration source criteria](../runtime-workflow/plan.md#complete-interoperability-and-migration-source-criteria) within this existing Open task. Preserve original criteria, historical review scopes and actual restrictions; current source/interface and implementation acceptance remain pending.\n\nL19 actual checked interop obligation handoff criterion (Open): Preserve current declared type/direction/provider/ABI/protocol/schema/profile/target/version, effects/grants, wrapper/unsafe/check/proof, ownership/lifetime/error/threading facts and source/generated/foreign provenance through common Core, MIR and lowering to the real runtime boundary. Actual compiler legality precedes admitted export; Runtime enforces it and cannot repair statically illegal source. Reject erased wrappers, stale proof/layout/host contracts, dropped translation/release and artifact records detached from their source. Required evidence: genuine producer/verifier/consumer accepted/refused artifacts and exact changed-subject preservation; no universal native execution or host bridge gates portable schema Core.\n<!-- legality-interop-source-handoff:end -->",
