compiletime/reproduce-hermetic-core`: Reproduce byte-identical typed core from declared semantic inputs in required hermetic release/conformance/publication/safety-critical modes, rejecting undeclared ambient inputs. Accept: In release, conformance, reproducible publication and safety-critical modes, repeat the same source/compiler/lock/target/grants/declared inputs and require byte-identical typed core. Declare environment key/value policy, pin or replay network/shell/model/tool/package inputs, record clock/random values or deterministic seeds, use declared target manifests and hash generated inputs. Native-object metadata differences require a marked nonsemantic field and target conformance acceptance. Reject: Reject undeclared filesystem/environment input, unrecorded nondeterminism, ambient target probing, typed-core drift or an unreviewed native-object exception; report L12-HERMETIC-INPUT or L12-NONDETERMINISM as applicable. Required outputs: Hermetic input/replay manifest, paired typed-core byte comparison, generated-input hashes, exception record when applicable and accepted/rejected diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from expand/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/expand5-integrate-generated-programs, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Criterion behavior/pkg11/explicit-target-fallback: accept Use a fallback target/runtime only when explicitly declared and compatible with project/profile/policy. Reject A failed target silently falls back to a different target or runtime. Emit Visible fallback selection in target/artifact records and PKG11007. Dependencies: PKG11, P13. Criterion behavior/pkg11/host-independent-cross-compile: accept Resolve and compile target profile/backend/runtime/ABI contracts independently of implicit host ABI, services and paths. Reject A cross build inherits host ABI/paths/default target assumptions. Emit Target-specific build/artifact identity and host-leakage rejection with PKG11002. Dependencies: PKG11, B1, R1. Criterion behavior/pkg11/per-target-evidence: accept Attach required conformance and support-level evidence separately to each target and expose every failing profile/target pair. Reject Default-target success hides a required target failure or a release claims support without its per-target conformance. Emit Per-target test/conformance reports, support table and PKG11006. Dependencies: PKG11, TEST3, TEST4, TEST6. Criterion behavior/pkg11/target-compatibility-admission: accept Validate profile/backend legality, dependency variants and capability availability for every concrete target before lowering. Reject A pair is unsupported, contradicts project profiles, lacks a dependency variant or assumes capabilities legal on another target. Emit Checked matrix, per-target graph/capability decision and PKG11001/PKG11003/PKG11004/PKG11008. Dependencies: PKG11, PKG5, P13, B1. Criterion behavior/pkg11/target-matrix-artifact: accept Normalize grouped declarations into concrete profile/backend/triple/ABI/calling-convention/runtime/features/dependency/capability/artifact/test/support entries and emit each target's manifests and support level. Reject Required target/ABI identity is missing, a matrix contradicts the project or a supported claim lacks its target-specific record. Emit Normalized matrix, dependency graph, capability summary, artifact/test/conformance manifests and supported/experimental/internal/build-only/unsupported table; PKG11005/PKG11008. Dependencies: PKG1, PKG11, R1, B1. Criterion behavior/pkg7/canonical-rebuild-comparison: accept Compare canonical manifests and actual content hashes for two locked builds under the same recipe, explaining only declared differences. Reject Verification compares filenames alone or ignores a changed canonical content/manifest identity. Emit Expected/actual digest lists and rebuild verification report; PKG7007. Dependencies: PKG3, PKG7. Criterion behavior/pkg7/deterministic-build-environment: accept Control source/project/lock/compiler/toolchain/graph/profile/target/environment/locale/timezone/order/timestamps/seeds/network/generated/blob/FFI inputs; normalize time/order/paths and seed or record randomness. Reject A reproducible build uses unlocked dependencies, unrecorded external reads/randomness, leaked host paths or generated source without generator/input hashes. Emit Controlled environment and input/output manifests, build recipe, exception list and PKG7002-PKG7006; changed compiler invalidates cache. Dependencies: PKG7, PKG2, PKG10. Criterion behavior/pkg7/nonreproducible-claim-boundary: accept Mark uncontrolled-input artifacts nonreproducible and list their exceptions explicitly. Reject A nonreproducible artifact satisfies a reproducible release/signing gate or a reproducibility claim lacks its recipe. Emit Nonreproducibility exception and release decision; PKG7001/PKG7008. Dependencies: PKG7, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg7/recorded-build-recipe: accept Emit a schema-valid release build recipe binding package/version, source/project/lock/compiler/toolchain, graph/task settings, concrete profile/target matrix, controlled environment/locale/timezone/traversal/timestamps/seeds/network, generator/input hashes, blobs/FFI inputs, expected artifact identities, output hashes and verification command or machine-readable equivalent. Rebuild twice under that exact recipe and compare canonical manifests and actual content hashes. For standard-library packages retain source commit, build graph, compiler, package lock, tests and policy-required signatures in the provenance record. Reject Reject a claimed reproducible release with no recipe, omitted or altered consumed inputs/outputs, unlocked dependencies, unrecorded network/randomness, host path leakage, missing generator hashes, filename-only comparison or unexplained hash drift; mark uncontrolled inputs nonreproducible and deny reproducible signing/release claims when policy requires reproducibility. Standard-library provenance and artifact identity must agree; neither API inventory nor a supplied success label proves a rebuild. Emit Versioned build-recipe artifact, controlled-environment manifest, input/output digest lists, actual repeat-build canonical comparison, exception list and PKG7001-PKG7008 diagnostics with recipe/input/artifact/target/environment context; standard-library source/build/lock/test/signature provenance links. Dependencies: PKG1/PKG2 project, lock and typed graph producers, PKG3 canonical manifests, PKG5 complete dependency lock, PKG10/PKG12 provenance/signing evidence, stdlib/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-platform-modules-and-close-release-manifests module/package manifests, BOOT6 trust evidence remains separate.\n<!-- build-canonical-recorded-rebuild:end -->\n\n<!-- authority-source-cache:start -->\n\nApply the [complete provider and capability source criteria](../auth-workflow/plan.md#complete-provider-and-capability-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; frozen finite reviews do not accept this whole-source/current implementation proposal.\n\nComplete provider reproducibility/cache consumer criterion (Open): Consume the existing dependency-aware cache task's actual provider-bound key, invalidation, reuse and rebuild-node products in repeated locked-build comparisons. That task remains the owner of shared/default cache construction and invalidation integration, including actual results from permitted L16 engine-specific cache machinery; this existing reproducibility task owns recorded recipe and actual canonical manifest/content comparisons across the claimed targets. Preserve selected provider id/version/scope/contract/trust/policy and compile-time input/output/replay identities in the consumed recipe/results, excluding secret values and enforcing the stable public cache-key secret policy. Changed provider/version/policy/contract or recorded inputs must be visible in the consumed cache decisions and recipe, preventing a stale reproducibility claim. A recorded replay exception alone grants no effect authority. Produce actual repeat-build comparisons and refused stale, mismatched, non-replayable or secret-leaking claims with source/build/compiler/provider identities; key-shaped metadata or a completed status is not reproducibility evidence.\n<!-- authority-source-cache:end -->\n\n\n<!-- compile-time-source-hermetic:start -->\n\nApply the [complete compile-time evaluation source criteria](../expand-workflow/plan.md#complete-compile-time-evaluation-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; finite reviewed source is not current whole-source or implementation acceptance.\n\nComplete L12 hermetic reproduction criterion (Open): In required release/conformance/reproducible-publication/safety-critical modes, repeat actual builds from identical source, compiler version, lockfile, target manifest, grants and declared inputs/replay records and compare byte-identical typed Core. Reject undeclared filesystem input; environment reads require the exact declared-key/explicit-value-policy premise under [Matt's declared/replayable-input decision](../../.specify/memory/constitution.md#hermetic-compile-time-inputs). Network/shell/model/tool use requires configured replayable provider or pinned result, clock/random requires recorded values or deterministic seed, probes use declared target manifests, and generated forms include input content hashes. A grant, replay exception or generic reproducible flag proves none of these premises. Native-object metadata variation needs an explicitly marked nonsemantic field and actual target-conformance acceptance; never relax typed-core equality. Consume actual cache results without implementing another cache, and retain unavailable/held cases, the authored/source-reviewed L6 clarification (`d2a0378bdd530857d97d530aab15268fc333ce80`) with its remaining authentication/`main`/implementation work (no historical L6 applying review renewed) and actual target evidence separately from signing/publication authority.\n<!-- compile-time-source-hermetic:end -->\n\n\n<!-- macro-source-rebuild:start -->\n\nApply the [complete macro source criteria](../expand-workflow/plan.md#complete-macro-source-criteria) within this existing task. Finite reviewed predicates remain scoped history; status and current independent acceptance do not change.\n\nComplete macro reproducibility consumer criterion (Open): Consume authentic engine/cache/event/value products and perform actual repeated declared-input builds and expansion-trace comparisons with source/compiler/provider/macro/grant/profile/target/facet/replay identity. Compare same-input hermetic typed-Core bytes under L12 separately from structural reference/alternative expansion equivalence under L16. Native metadata exceptions retain their explicitly marked nonsemantic fields and target acceptance; never weaken typed-Core equality. Retain actual cache invalidation/refusal and secret-safe recipe/output evidence without implementing another cache, issuing authority or treating records as reproducibility results.\n<!-- macro-source-rebuild:end -->\n\n\n\n\n<!-- library-base-source-recipe:start -->\n\nApply the [complete library foundation criteria](../stdlib-workflow/plan.md#complete-library-foundation-source-criteria) within this existing task. Preserve its status, partial evidence, prior predicates and actual restrictions; current whole-source/interface acceptance remains pending.\n\nLibrary foundation recipe criterion (Open): Produce the actual standard-library release recipe and repeat-build comparison over controlled source/project/lock/compiler/toolchain/graph/profile/target/environment/locale/timezone/order/timestamp/seed/network/generated/blob/FFI inputs and output identities. Record permitted nondeterminism and policy exceptions and bind actual canonical content/manifests rather than filenames or supplied matching hashes. Refuse missing/changed/unrecorded inputs and false reproducibility. Evidence: real locked build recipes, actual repeated content/manifest comparisons, invalidation and exact package/STD1 refusals; future signed outputs are no first recipe inputs.\n<!-- library-base-source-recipe:end -->\n\n\n\n<!-- build-interop-source-reproducibility:start -->\n\nApply the [complete interoperability and migration source criteria](../runtime-workflow/plan.md#complete-interoperability-and-migration-source-criteria) within this existing Open task. Preserve original criteria, historical review scopes and actual restrictions; current source/interface and implementation acceptance remain pending.\n\nL19 actual versioned binding and artifact reproducibility criterion (Open): Repeat selected real declared generation/builds from the same authentic incumbent/schema/provider/compiler/target/lock and permitted effect inputs, comparing actual binding/codecs/metadata/provenance artifacts under the governing reproducibility contract. Versioned labels and assigned reproducible flags do not establish equality, compatibility, privacy or incumbent parity. Preserve accurate source identity even where selected semantic outputs are stable; unavailable inputs cannot pass. Required evidence: genuine repeated locked-build/generation comparisons and changed-input/missing-source negatives, with final selfhost/release equivalence and authorized signing/publication remaining separate.\n<!-- build-interop-source-reproducibility:end -->",
