  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-runtime-conformance-fixtures` Execute runtime conformance fixtures\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST3](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/192-test3-runtime-test-strategy.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute runtime conformance fixtures runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source testing/test3/ai-ledger: Test and reconstruct runtime model/prompt/tool/memory/policy/human-review/replay events using model/tool ledgers. Concrete acceptance: Run model/tool/memory/policy/review/replay fixtures and delete or alter one causal ledger event; reconstruction must fail and unauthorized operations must remain denied. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/capability-denial: Deny runtime operations with missing grants and execute fixtures without ambient host services or authority. Concrete acceptance: Exercise the same runtime operation with its exact grant and with absent, narrowed or revoked grants; observe denial before the side effect and reject ambient authority. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/concurrency: Test runtime scheduling, synchronization, actors and race-prevention claims. Concrete acceptance: Exercise scheduler, synchronization, actors and supported race-prevention claims; inject an invalid synchronization or ownership edge and require the specified rejection/check failure rather than a clean concurrency report. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/family-coverage: Exercise positive and negative fixtures separately for all declared runtime families, recording family/profile/target/artifact and runtime version. Concrete acceptance: Omit or misidentify a claimed no-runtime/minimal/managed/memory/concurrency/distributed/AI/REPL/FFI/capability/observability family; fail coverage and separate unsupported cases from executed passes. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/ffi-boundary: Test FFI ABI identity, ownership, errors, callbacks and cleanup and reject mismatched ABI. Concrete acceptance: Use mismatched ABI identity, ownership transfer, error normalization, callback lifetime or cleanup behavior; the FFI fixture must reject or expose the specified failure and verify cleanup on error. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/memory-safety: Test runtime allocation, deallocation, arenas, regions and unsafe wrappers where supported. Concrete acceptance: Exercise supported allocation/deallocation/arena/region/unsafe-wrapper boundaries, including invalid lifetime, double release and missing audit controls; fail unsafe outcomes or unsupported claims. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/observability: Validate runtime event schemas and redaction without secret leakage. Concrete acceptance: Inject a secret/no-store value and an event with wrong schema or identity; require redaction or refusal and fail any secret-bearing or schema-invalid report. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/replay: Test distributed retry/idempotency/compensation/event logs with recorded nondeterminism; replay must not repeat side effects. Concrete acceptance: Record a retry/idempotency/compensation/event-log run, replay it, then remove nondeterministic events or repeat an external effect; fail replay equivalence and assert no duplicated side effect. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/report: Emit runtime conformance, capability decision, memory safety, concurrency, replay, AI ledger, FFI and observability reports linked to artifact/profile/target/runtime version. Concrete acceptance: Omit a required runtime/capability/memory/concurrency/replay/AI/FFI/observability report or change its artifact/profile/target/runtime version; reject unrelated or incomplete conformance evidence. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. This producer supplies conformance evidence; independent intermediate admission and final release remain separate consumers. Current implementation acceptance is unassessed.",
