  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-agent-and-workflow-evaluations` Execute agent and workflow evaluations\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST8](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/197-test8-ai-and-workflow-evaluation-strategy.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute agent and workflow evaluations runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source testing/test8/human-review: Evaluate human-review grant/deny/expiry/revocation/payload-change behavior. Concrete acceptance: Execute grant, deny, expiry, revocation and payload-change cases with the same action identity; deny stale or mismatched approval and fail missing refusal cases. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test8/metric-release: Apply declared metric thresholds to deterministic release decisions and fail closed for missing or stale evaluation evidence. Concrete acceptance: Score the declared dataset under explicit thresholds, then remove/stale the subject-bound eval or cross the threshold; require deterministic fail-closed release decisions. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test8/report: Emit evaluation, dataset, scored output, replay, tool/memory, human-review, safety, budget and release-gate artifacts linked to release gates. Concrete acceptance: Remove or alter subject/dataset/model/prompt/tool/memory/policy/runtime, scored output, replay,