  "- [ ] `resolve/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/resolve5-integrate-binding-consumers` resolve/5: Integrate binding consumers\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Connect Core/Types and diagnostic/LSP consumers; demonstrate accepted shadowing and imports plus rejected ambiguity, visibility, cycle and stale-export cases.\n\n\n<!-- resolve-source-consumers:start -->\n\nApply the [complete namespace and resolution source criteria](plan.md#complete-namespace-and-resolution-source-criteria) within this existing task. Preserve its Open status, original criteria and historical evidence scope.\n\nC5/L3 consumer/conformance criterion (Open): Connect actual C3/C4 expanded-context and L1/L2 namespace-form inputs, explicit package/profile/foreign artifacts and resulting bindings to Core/Types/Effects/Auth/profile checks, package graphs, documentation/LSP and incremental consumers. Namespace tables precede expansion where required by L3; final symbol binding follows expanded positions under C5, and unresolved references cannot enter Types. Declared type/effect/authority records remain distinct from actual later inference/legality results; all required module summaries and facts must be current before target consumption. Required outputs: real producer/consumer and serialization/invalidation results covering every C5/L3 resolution position, stable binding identity, single-profile/multi-profile library exclusions, public/private and foreign imports, legal/refused shadowing, graph/cross-profile/target/capability cases and source-free package graph derivation. Preserve all ten C5 diagnostic meanings and all eight L3 meanings, with symbol/syntax ID/span/namespace/profile/target/candidate-bindings-when-applicable/dependency-edge/remediation context. Namespace-rule changes require conformance-fixture updates and package compatibility review under their owning policies; this source reconciliation changes no language rule. Preserve the separate frozen owner source-to-Core verification package and its finite scope. These are future implementation/evidence requirements, not current resolver/module/profile/package/runtime/probe execution, whole-component acceptance or independent source approval.\n<!-- resolve-source-consumers:end -->",
