  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-fuzz-and-property-fixtures` Execute fuzz and property fixtures\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST9](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/198-test9-fuzzing-and-property-testing-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute fuzz and property fixtures runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source testing/test9/live-effect-policy: Use recorded/mocked provider/tool effects for AI/workflow fuzzing; prohibit unbudgeted live provider calls and live effects without policy. Concrete acceptance: Run recorded/mocked AI/workflow cases; attempt a live effect without explicit credential/external billing/retention policy and require denial before the call. No compiler work allowance may substitute for external-service policy. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test9/minimize-regressions: Minimize failures into reproducible cases and promote shrunk reproducers to regression fixtures. Concrete acceptance: Inject a reproducible failure, shrink it while preserving the failure oracle, and rerun the promoted regression; fail absent minimization, changed failure cause or missing compiler/oracle outputs. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test9/mir-preservation: Check MIR and optimization preservation properties with generated inputs. Concrete acceptance: Generate valid and deliberately invalid MIR/pass transformations with declared facts; detect lost types/effects/ownership/safety/origins and reject an unsound preservation claim. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test9/property-oracle: Execute generated property cases against their declared expected invariant and failure oracle, retaining attributable replayable input and result evidence. Concrete acceptance: Execute generated cases against the declared invariant and oracle, including a known violating input; fail missing oracle, fabricated pass flags or evidence unrelated to the replayable input. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test9/replay-identity: Record fuzz seed, generator version, profile/target/compiler and shrinker so generated source/schema/MIR/math/package/workflow/runtime cases replay in CI. Concrete acceptance: Replay from seed/generator/shrinker/compiler/profile/target identities and compare complete cases/results; missing or changed identities must fail reproducibility rather than silently using a new generator. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test9/report: Emit seed corpus, generated case manifest, property/coverage/crash reports, minimized reproducer and promoted regression fixture with profile/target identities. Concrete acceptance: Remove seed corpus, generated manifest, property/coverage/crash report, minimized reproducer or regression promotion required by the run; reject reports with absent profile/target or untraceable cases. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test9/schema-canonicalization: Check schema validation and canonicalization under generated values. Concrete acceptance: Generate valid/invalid schemas and values, checking validator outcomes and canonical round trips; detect malformed values, canonical collisions or changed semantics rather than trusting serialization success. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test9/valid-invalid: Accept generated valid programs or report known resource-limit diagnostics; invalid programs produce stable diagnostics rather than compiler crashes, preserving type/effect invariants. Concrete acceptance: Run generated valid and invalid programs through the real compiler; fail crashes, missing stable diagnostics and type/effect violations. Any known resource diagnostic must identify an actual host/platform restriction, never revive removed input/work quotas; retain the TEST9 source-policy exception explicitly. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. This producer supplies conformance evidence; independent intermediate admission and final release remain separate consumers. Current implementation acceptance is unassessed.",
