  "- [ ] `mir/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/mir1-construct-semantic-mir` mir/1: Construct semantic MIR\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Lower checked-core control flow, calls/closures, data, memory/regions/resources, errors, FFI/concurrency and declared domain/workflow/AI operations without target-specific instructions.\n\n<!-- mir-canonical-construction:start -->\nApply the [complete MIR source criteria](plan.md#complete-mir-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; current independent review and implementation acceptance are pending.\n\nC11 construction criterion compiler/c11/semantic-mir-construction (Open): Construct the canonical target-independent MIR module/function/block/operation records from checked core, exposing control-flow and data-flow graphs and stable artifact identities. Cover the complete C11 families: constants/locals/block arguments; calls/tail calls/closures and direct/dictionary/vtable/dynamic dispatch; records/structs/tuples/enums/unions and field/index/slice/buffer operations; arithmetic/conversions; allocation/initialization/load/store/move/drop; region/arena and linear-resource lifecycle; branches/loops/matches and errors; FFI/host boundaries; atomics/locks/channels/tasks/synchronization; workflow suspension/resume/events; AI model/tool/memory/policy; domain anchors; runtime checks and proof/certificate references. Every operation has opcode, operands, result, type, effects/order, source/generated origin, profile and verifier status with applicable fact references; no-result operations use nil result and Unit or bottom as appropriate. Blocks have ordered operations and exactly one legal C11 terminator, including proof-qualified unreachable, profile-legal suspend/yield and legal tail call. SSA values or block arguments may represent joins, but public data-flow edges remain explicit. The module references actual checked core, profile, target request, functions/globals and metadata/anchor tables; functions retain parameters, return type, latent effects, entry/blocks and origin. A target request may constrain legality but cannot redefine opcode semantics. Required outputs: actual MIR/CFG/DFG, origin and anchor records plus operation-family/schema coverage fixtures under declared profiles. Reject malformed records/joins, missing required operation fields and target-specific instruction semantics in generic MIR with applicable C11-MODULE/BLOCK/TARGET-LEAK diagnostics. Positive construction produces verifiable artifacts, not a fabricated verifier success.\n<!-- mir-canonical-construction:end -->",
