  "- [ ] `types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core` types/5: Integrate typed core\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Feed Effects and MIR prerequisites from actual solutions, with accepted inferred/declared cases and rejected unsatisfied, stale and illegal-conversion cases.\n\n\n<!-- types-source-verification:start -->\n\nApply the [complete Types source criteria](plan.md#complete-types-source-criteria) within this existing Open task. Preserve original criteria and exact historical review scopes. This restores already-published planning text; the original C7 publication operation, implementation reservations and all execution restrictions remain unchanged.\n\nC7/L5 typed-core verifier and consumer criterion (Open): Verify after actual expansion/name resolution/Core production and before Effects can claim legality that each node has exactly one current type or diagnostic, all constraints are solved or rejected, function latent effects are present, all nontrivial conversions have cast records, Dynamic boundaries are profile-marked, schema-derived types reference source schemas, required layout facts exist and source/generated origins survive. Malformed typed-core artifacts refuse with C7-VERIFY and prevent downstream legality claims. Typed core feeds actual Effects and ownership/safety/profile/capability validation; it is not target-lowering authority until those required checks pass. MIR/lowering fixtures must preserve the checked type facts and generic/dispatch/schema/boundary contracts; actual later checks consume current artifacts, not fabricated summaries or completed-component prerequisites. Required outputs: positive typed-core emission for literals, calls, functions, records, unions, matches, protocols, generics, dynamic/schema/ownership/linear surfaces; deterministic constraint/annotation diagnostics; accepted/rejected boundary, cast/unsafe, layout/schema, stale-ar