  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/obtain-independent-acceptance-for-the-exact-release-candidate` Obtain independent acceptance for the exact release candidate\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Binary release gates](../../docs/phase-18-binary-distribution-and-seedless-release/IMPLEMENTATION-ROADMAP.md)\n\n<!-- release-parent-acceptance:start -->\nAdditional proposed source criteria (Open), from the published Release\n[task source](https://github.com/burn2delete/uniform/blob/df11890b21f71d3f246cc47e9f63d866239a0d68/specs/release-workflow/tasks.md).\nThe following closing-evidence text is preserved verbatim; the original\ncriterion below and existing governance interfaces remain required.\n\nCoordinator-reviewed candidate receipts and explicit release disposition BOOT1/BOOT3/BOOT5/BOOT6/BOOT8: For this exact release candidate, consume fresh source-bound claimed-stage/module conformance, equivalence, compatibility, provenance, TCB and applicable unsafe-audit evidence. Reject failing declared conformance, missing or stale evidence, unreviewed claimed-support gaps and revoked inputs. Preserve policy-qualified reproducibility exceptions. Intermediate stage/module authoritative admission is the separate consumer proposed under release task2 (complete-stage-compatibilityequivalence-across-the-claimed-compiler); ordinary development and final release acceptance remain separate from that migration decision. The task2 interface and executable evidence remain Open until canonically composed and independently accepted. This release gate does not implement compiler passes, native seed ABIs or their tests. Release extension release/candidate-eligibility-failclosed: Assess the exact final candidate against P15 retirement and applicable P18 public commands, four-boundary seed exclusion, full self-hosted conformance, rebuild and provenance/SBOM/signing/target/compatibility/security/governance evidence. Exercise eligible success and every missing/false/stale/corrupt evidence refusal with stable owning P18 blockers. Under-evidenced candidates remain incomplete and bin/gravity retains labelled packaged fallback. Preserve intermediate admission and ordinary development separately; supplied manifests cannot confer final eligibility.\n<!-- release-parent-acceptance:end -->\n\nClosing evidence: Coordinator-reviewed candidate receipts and explicit release disposition",
